Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to kernel/sched/core.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    threads (and processes) at once     32 -> 16 (the table: 26 -> 13 KiB)
    kernel stack of a thread/process    16 KiB -> 4 KiB (one per process,
                                        from the kernel heap; the kernel
                                        paths a process can reach here
                                        have no FAT and no SD driver)
    the reaper's stack                  8 KiB -> 3 KiB
tests/nrf52/renode_session.sh reports the largest kernel stack a process
used (reap_kstack_max) after the shell session.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/kernel/sched/core.ad --label b/kernel/sched/core.ad kernel/sched/core.ad <copy>

--- a/kernel/sched/core.ad
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.ad
@@ -36,12 +36,12 @@
 from kernel.mpu import mpu_switch
 from board.board import board_tick_start
 
-THREAD_MAX: uint32 = 32
+THREAD_MAX: uint32 = 16                # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 32
 SCHED_PRIOS: uint32 = 8
 SCHED_HZ: uint32 = 1000
 SCHED_SLICE: uint32 = 10
 STACK_GUARD: uint32 = 1024         # no-access MPU region at the bottom of a stack
-KSTACK_DEFAULT: uint32 = 16384
+KSTACK_DEFAULT: uint32 = 4096          # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 16384
 STACK_FILL: uint32 = 0xA5A5A5A5
 
 T_UNUSED: uint32 = 0
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@
     name: Array[16, uint8]
 
 
-threads: Array[32, Thread]
+threads: Array[16, Thread]
 sched_current: uint64 = 0           # Ptr[Thread]; read by switch.S
 sched_running: uint32 = 0
 sched_ticks: volatile uint64 = 0
@@ -958,7 +958,7 @@
     sched_running = 0
     wq_init(&reaper_wq)
     thread_create("idle", cast[uint64](&_idle_main), 0, SCHED_PRIOS - 1, 2048, 0)
-    thread_create("reaper", cast[uint64](&_reaper_main), 0, SCHED_PRIOS - 2, 8192, 0)
+    thread_create("reaper", cast[uint64](&_reaper_main), 0, SCHED_PRIOS - 2, 3072, 0)
 
 
